# =============================================================
# Local data — never versioned
# =============================================================

# SQLite database plus its WAL/SHM sidecars. Per spec-modelo-de-datos.md the
# database is a single file mounted as a Docker volume: it is local state,
# rebuildable from the seed CSV. Committing it would also leak reading data.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# Docker volume directory for the database file.
# Contents ignored, directory kept so the volume mount point exists on clone.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# =============================================================
# Personal data
# =============================================================

# The filled seed CSV is my real reading list (data/seed.csv per
# spec-seed-manual.md). Blanket-ignore every CSV, then re-include only the
# versioned template. spec-seed-manual.md fixes its name as seed-plantilla.csv;
# the generic patterns are kept so a renamed template still works.
*.csv
!seed-plantilla.csv
!*-plantilla.csv
!*.template.csv
!*.example.csv
!*-template.csv
!*-example.csv

# =============================================================
# Secrets
# =============================================================

# Telegram bot token and chat id.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template

# =============================================================
# Source fixtures
# =============================================================

# Raw audit dumps from manganato (samples/, catalogued in section 10 of
# manganato-fuente-actual.md). A single feed page is ~155 KB and every file
# here is re-downloadable, so the whole folder stays out by default.
#
# Two ways to keep parse-test fixtures:
#   - preferred: trimmed fixtures under tests/fixtures/, which is versioned;
#   - or un-ignore specific files here, e.g.
#       !samples/api_chapters_accidental-romance.json
samples/*

# =============================================================
# Throwaway exploration
# =============================================================

# Disposable scripts that are not part of the application — the feed-window
# measurement script is the reference case. Kept out deliberately so nothing
# here can be mistaken for application code.
scratchpad/
scratch/
explore/

# =============================================================
# Python
# =============================================================

# Bytecode caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Build and packaging artifacts
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Test, coverage and type-check caches
.pytest_cache/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/blob-report/
.tox/
.nox/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Stray log files. Application logging goes to stdout by design
# (see the logging strategy in spec-modelo-de-datos.md).
*.log

# =============================================================
# Operating system
# =============================================================

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# =============================================================
# Agent tooling
# =============================================================

# Auto-generated skill index. Contains absolute paths from one machine's
# home directory, so it is neither portable nor useful to anyone else.
# Regenerate with: gentle-ai skill-registry refresh --force
.atl/

# Personal Claude Code settings for this checkout. Holds the Stop hook that
# pushes this project's memories to a self-hosted Engram cloud — one owner's
# infrastructure and token, useless and confusing to anyone else, so it is
# ignored by name rather than by ignoring the whole directory: a shared
# `.claude/settings.json` remains versionable if one is ever needed.
.claude/settings.local.json

# =============================================================
# Editors and IDEs
# =============================================================
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Session.vim
.netrwhist

# impeccable's generated design context. Ignored by decision (2026-08-21):
# PRODUCT.md would be a second source of product truth competing with docs/,
# which is Spanish and authoritative. A tool-generated English doc nobody owns
# drifts, and stale documents are this repo's most expensive recurring defect.
PRODUCT.md
.impeccable/
